      "text": [
        {
          "id": "title",
          "visible": true,
          "kicker": "#2 · Aion chs. VI–IX (§§127–187)",
          "title": "The fishes give the age its temporal image",
          "italic": "The doubled figure embodies an age living its contrary tendencies successively while the constellational image holds them together — an inherited forecast is not a confirmed causal law of history.",
          "body": "",
          "x": 0.04,
          "y": 0.05,
          "width": 560,
          "size": 30,
          "align": "left"
        },
        {
          "id": "body1",
          "visible": true,
          "kicker": "",
          "title": "",
          "italic": "",
          "body": "Jung opens the fish inquiry by noting that Christian interpretation gives Christ and the devil several shared animal symbols: a symbol can carry more than one valuation. The Christian fish has its baptismal, eucharistic and epigraphic settings; astrology is proposed as a second source of its activation. Pisces lets the double figure acquire duration: planetary conjunctions, messianic calculations, medieval expectations and the precessional movement of the spring-point — Jung's own notes sometimes correct his authorities' astronomy, and an inherited forecast is not an independently confirmed law. The Pistis Sophia narrative gives doubling a reunion",
          "x": 0.04,
          "y": 0.47,
          "width": 620,
          "size": 14,
          "align": "left",
          "w": 520
        },
        {
          "id": "body2",
          "visible": true,
          "kicker": "",
          "title": "",
          "italic": "",
          "body": "form: the child-double bound to a bed, released on the fathers' return, embraced, one — its office distinct from Christ/Antichrist antagonism. The sixteenth century sharpens the pressure: schism and the conquest of Nature cross the earlier aspiration; Nostradamus's letter makes expectation itself a historical actor. Epiphanius's Alexandrian rite — the image carried up, circled, returned below — is a pagan rite Jung uses as testimony. The apocalyptic Lamb resists a single label; Leviathan's traditions split monster against monster until the formidable creature becomes food for the devout — terror, opposition and nourishment as successive offices.\n\nOccurrences: the shared animal symbols (#2); the precessional calculations (#2, historicised at #5→0); the embracing double (#2); Leviathan's conversion into meal (#2, distinct from the authored Meal whole).",
          "x": 0.6,
          "y": 0.47,
          "width": 505,
          "size": 14,
          "align": "left"
        }
      ],
