      "text": [
        {
          "id": "title",
          "visible": true,
          "kicker": "#4 · Aion chs. XIII–XV (§§287–427; the quaternio at §§402–421)",
          "title": "The quaternio — Anthropos, Shadow, Physis, lapis",
          "italic": "Jung's schema demonstrates a dynamic process within the Self — and the project's reading of the diamonds stays Offered with human-amplified: no: the Shadow's field is not the Anthropos field relabelled.",
          "body": "",
          "x": 0.04,
          "y": 0.05,
          "width": 560,
          "size": 30,
          "align": "left"
        },
        {
          "id": "body1",
          "visible": true,
          "kicker": "",
          "title": "",
          "italic": "",
          "body": "The Gnostic return reaches back before the era's images of attraction: the Naassene water of doctrine, the Peratic serpent-Son conveying signs down and carrying their awakened substance up, Monoïmos's instruction to investigate the one who speaks of \"my\" spirit. The concluding quaternio makes the historical interpretation answerable: Jung explicitly acknowledges that his inserted Shadow Quaternio is a modern reconstruction absent from the Gnostic texts, supplied because a purely upward orientation no longer describes the modern situation — the disappointment of the expected return, increased self-consciousness, the",
          "x": 0.04,
          "y": 0.47,
          "width": 620,
          "size": 14,
          "align": "left",
          "w": 520
        },
        {
          "id": "body2",
          "visible": true,
          "kicker": "",
          "title": "",
          "italic": "",
          "body": "chthonic serpent, the approach to Nature. The four major states are Anthropos A, Shadow B, Physis/serpent C, lapis D, with lower-case transformations; at p.259 the connected diamonds show each whole unfolding into four and passing onward. The ring returns through differentiation and integration — solve et coagula, the circular opus — changing an unconscious totality into a conscious one; the nuclear comparison stays explicitly hypothetical. The conclusion returns to the clinician's first encounter: the shadow includes healthy instincts and creative capacities; declaring all things good leaves suffering untouched.\n\nOccurrences: the declared modern reconstruction of the Shadow (#4, keeping the project's Offered reading honest); the connected diamonds (p.259); the conclusion's responsibility (#1, #4).",
          "x": 0.6,
          "y": 0.47,
          "width": 505,
          "size": 14,
          "align": "left"
        }
      ],
